.TH UI 4
.SH NAME
ui \- a window of widgets, described through files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ui
[
.B -s
.I srvname
]
.PP
.B mount /srv/ui.\fIuser\fP.\fIpid\fP /mnt/ui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ui
runs in a window of
.IR wsys (4)
or
.IR rio (1)
and shows there what a client describes: a tree of widgets (rows, columns,
labels, buttons, text boxes, check boxes, progress bars, sliders, scrolled
and sized boxes).
The client writes the tree and reads what the user did; the widgets, their
state (focus, the text being edited, scrolling) and their layout stay in
.IR ui ,
as an
.IR acme (4)
window's text stays in acme.
The files are 9P: a client on another machine mounts them as well
.RI ( import (4)).
.PP
.I Ui
posts its files in
.BI /srv/ srvname
(default
.BI ui. user . pid\fR,
printed on standard output); the entry goes with
.IR ui .
Its widgets are Masonry's (linebender), drawn by the processor (vello_cpu):
no GPU is needed.
It takes its fonts from
.BR /lib/font/ttf .
.SS Files
.TF nodes/id/children
.TP
.B ctl
Written: a transaction, the lines of one write applied all or none (an error
names the line); read: where the window's contents are on the screen,
.IR "x y width height" .
.TP
.B event
Read: what the user did, a line each, from the open on:
.BI click " id" ,
.BI text " id text"
(a text box changed),
.BI enter " id text" ,
.BI check " id " 0 \fR|\fP 1\fR,
.BI slide " id value" ,
.BR close .
A read waits for one; a flush (an interrupt) ends the wait.
.TP
.B tree
The tree in
.BR ctl 's
language: written to
.B ctl
it makes the same scene.
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /kind
The node's kind.
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /props
Its properties,
.I key value
a line; written:
.B set
for each line.
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /children
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /rect
Where it is in the window,
.I x0 y0 x1 y1
(as the last frame had it).
.PD
.SS Ctl's language
.TF "move id parent [index]"
.TP
.BI new " id kind \fR[\fPparent \fR[\fPindex\fR]]"
A node of a kind:
.BR column ,
.BR row ,
.BR label ,
.BR button ,
.BR textbox ,
.BR checkbox ,
.BR progress ,
.BR slider ,
.B scroll
(one child),
.B box
(one child or none); in
.I parent
(default
.BR root ,
a column) at
.I index
(default: the end).
Ids are letters, digits and
.BR _-. .
.TP
.BI set " id key value"
A property; the value is the rest of the line (in rc's quotes if it starts or
ends with blanks):
.B text
(label, button, text box, check box),
.B placeholder
(text box),
.B checked
(0 or 1),
.B value
(progress: 0 to 1 or
.BR none ;
slider),
.BR min ,
.BR max ,
.B step
(slider),
.BR width ,
.B height
(box, in pixels),
.B flex
(a child's share of its row or column),
.B gap
and
.B align
.RB ( start ,
.BR center ,
.BR end :
across a row or column).
.TP
.BI del " id
The node and what is under it.
.TP
.BI move " id parent \fR[\fPindex\fR]
.TP
.BI title " text
.TP
.B clear
All but the root.
.PD
.PP
The user's changes go into the tree as well: a text box's
.BR text ,
a check box's
.BR checked ,
a slider's
.BR value .
.SH EXAMPLES
A window with a button, from rc:
.IP
.EX
window 'ui -s hello'
mount /srv/hello /mnt/ui
echo 'new b button
set b text press me' >/mnt/ui/ctl
cat /mnt/ui/event	# click b, when it is pressed
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/ui
(Rust; Masonry, winit and softbuffer with their plan9 backends:
.BR /sys/src/rust )
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ui (2)
(the files from C),
.IR uiview (2)
(from Rust, views of a program's state),
.IR wsys (4),
.IR rio (4),
.IR acme (4)
.SH BUGS
One window an
.IR ui .
Deleting the window ends
.I ui
with a note: the clients' reads of
.B event
end without
.BR close .
A change of the tree's shape makes all widgets again (the focus is lost);
properties change the widgets in place.
